@startuml
!include ../../_style.iuml
' Derived from crates/openmeet-intel/src/vad.rs (VadConfig::from_settings: min_speech_ms = 150 - 50 x sensitivity
' (120 ms at the default 0.6), pre_roll_ms 240, silence_ms from settings (default 700), min_utterance_ms 350,
' max_utterance_ms 20000; Segmenter::push emits SpeechStarted / Utterance / Discarded),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/transcription.rs (SegmenterEvent -> TranscriptionEvent::SpeechStarted / SpeechEnded,
' transcribe_final), crates/openmeet-engine/src/conversation.rs (handle_final arms TurnTimer,
' on_integrity_timer, on_turn_timer, SpeechStarted bumps turn.version), crates/openmeet-engine/src/integrity.rs
' (on_candidate_segment returns Timer with turn_end_silence_ms; on_candidate_speech_started bumps version),
' crates/openmeet-core/src/settings.rs (turn_end_silence_ms default 1500; silence_ms default 700).
' Times are illustrative (ASR latency is not drawn); the rules and default values are the code's.
title Candidate turn in interviewer mode: VAD, transcription and the two turn-end timers (defaults)

concise "Candidate voice" as V
concise "Segmenter" as S
concise "Final text" as F
concise "Turn and integrity timers" as T

@0
V is speech
S is idle
F is none
T is none

@120
S is speaking

@2600
V is silent

@3300
S is ended

@3800
F is "text 1"
T is "armed 1500 ms"

@4200
V is speech

@4320
S is speaking
T is "bumped timer 1 outdated"

@5000
V is silent

@5700
S is ended

@6200
F is "text 2"
T is "armed 1500 ms"

@7700
T is "fired no speech"
S is idle

@8000
T is "check runs"
@enduml
